Modifications implement Orca's gVisor + in-sandbox FUSE-only contract:

- BatchSandboxProvider initialization requires secure_runtime.type=gvisor and
  secure_runtime.k8s_runtime_class=gvisor.
- Isolation requests require both bootstrap.execd.isolation=enable and
  orca.fuse.device=enable, plus exact operator-owned image + entrypoint trust.
- Generated Pods use runtimeClassName=gvisor, add only SETFCAP and SYS_ADMIN for isolation,
  and reject privileged containers, hostPath volumes, host namespaces,
  hostUsers, procMount, pool mode, and Windows workloads.
- FUSE uses gVisor's virtual /dev/fuse; no host /dev/fuse mount exists.
- Pause and resume reject before any BatchSandbox CR patch.
- Security-context conversion preserves seccomp and AppArmor profiles without
  adding procMount handling.

Dockerfile build-input hardening remains separate at
services/harness-server/sandbox-templates/orca-opensandbox-server/.

